From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:39:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: rpi: console output on serial only

NextBSD boots the Raspberry Pi 5 family silently: from the firmware to
the login window nothing but the boot splash reaches the screen
(nextbsd/nextbsd#542). U-Boot's board environment sends stdout and
stderr to the HDMI screen as well as the serial port, so everything
U-Boot prints before it starts loader.efi (the PCIe link line from
"pci enum", the "load" and "bootefi" messages) is drawn on the screen.

Print to the serial port only. The display is still probed, so
loader.efi gets its EFI GOP framebuffer, and NextBSD's bootcmd switches
the screen back on before it prints a failure.

NextBSD-only; not for upstream.
---
 board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env
index 6104f3b1..d7537fd2 100644
--- a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env
+++ b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env
@@ -6,8 +6,8 @@ dhcpuboot=usb start; dhcp u-boot.uimg; bootm
 
 /* Environment */
 stdin=serial,usbkbd
-stdout=serial,vidconsole
-stderr=serial,vidconsole
+stdout=serial
+stderr=serial
 
 /* DFU over USB/UDC */
 #ifdef CONFIG_CMD_DFU
